<title>INDIA: Fall in 1st half earnings growth for Indian firms.</title>
<headline>Fall in 1st half earnings growth for Indian firms.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is an analysis of first half results of 181 Indian firms announced until November 19. The analysis by R. Balakrishnan, president at securities firm Dil Vikas Finance Ltd shows that Indian companies have recorded a fall in earnings growth for the first time in four years.</p>
<p>The analysis classifies firms by their ownership patterns (state-run, multinationals, GDR and others), except for the finance sector which forms a separate group.</p>
<p>		 AN ANALYSIS OF HALF-YEARLY RESULTS</p>
<p>(figures in rupees million, unless stated otherwise)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>		   FINANCE     GDR   MNCS    PSUS    OTHERS   TOTAL</p>
<p>No. of Cos.	    9	22	27	 8	115     187</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Sales 9/95	 24702  198851   39060  115799   76608   455020</p>
<p>Sales 9/96	 31849  239041   49592  123447   94657   538586</p>
<p>Change(%)	    29%     20%     27%	7%     24%	18%</p>
<p>Othr.Inc</p>
<p>    Sep-95	   362    6826    1218     882    1893    11181</p>
<p>    Sep-96	   144    7613    1060    1204    2349    12370</p>
<p>Change(%)	   -60%     12%    -13%     37%     24%	11%</p>
<p>Depr.</p>
<p>    Sep-95		    7583     895    1991    2624    13093</p>
<p>    Sep-96		   10153    1190    2715    3223    17281</p>
<p>Change(%)			34%     33%     36%     23%	32%</p>
